  "markdown_content": "## Policy Reversal\\nSecretary of State Marco Rubio has signed a declaration invoking emergency authorities to expedite approximately $4 billion in military assistance to Israel. The action marks a reversal of what was described as the Biden Administration's partial arms embargo, which had withheld certain weapons and ammunition from Israel.\\n\\n## Military Support\\nThe Trump Administration has demonstrated its commitment to Israel's security by approving nearly $12 billion in major Foreign Military Sales (FMS) to Israel since taking office. This latest decision accompanies President Trump's repeal of a Biden-era memorandum that had placed what officials called \"baseless and politicized conditions\" on military assistance to Israel during a period when the ally was engaged in conflicts against Iran and terror proxies on multiple fronts.\\n\\n## Ongoing Commitment\\nThe Administration has pledged to continue utilizing all available tools to uphold America's long-standing commitment to Israel's security, including measures to counter security threats.",
